Enforcement Guidelines / Consequences
Consequences follow a progressive framework based on the severity and frequency of violations:
Correction: Private written warning, clarification of the violation, possible public apology
Warning: Formal warning with restrictions on interactions; continued violations may lead to bans
Temporary Ban: Suspension from community interactions for a specified period; no contact with affected parties
Permanent Ban: Permanent removal from participation due to repeated or severe violations, harassment, or aggression toward groups or individuals 
